From a09e9079fdbff7c0da684776abe25ed126ee541b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:07:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zephyr: tcp: time out reads with poll() when SO_RCVTIMEO is
 unavailable

zenoh-pico runs the read and lease jobs on one executor thread
(zp_start_lease_task is a no-op). _z_tcp_zephyr_open sets SO_RCVTIMEO, but
Zephyr rejects it unless CONFIG_NET_CONTEXT_RCVTIMEO is set, and the failure
is only logged. recv() then blocks until data arrives, the lease job never
runs, no keep-alive is sent while the peer is quiet, and the router expires
the session after one lease.

Without CONFIG_NET_CONTEXT_RCVTIMEO, poll for Z_CONFIG_SOCKET_TIMEOUT before
recv() and return SIZE_MAX on timeout, which the client read job already
treats as "nothing to read". With it, SO_RCVTIMEO works and nothing changes.

Enabling CONFIG_NET_CONTEXT_RCVTIMEO is not always an option: on an ESP32
board it stopped the system in early boot, before WiFi init.

Signed-off-by: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
---
 src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c b/src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c
index 957471a6..d7973550 100644
--- a/src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c
+++ b/src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c
@@ -192,6 +192,13 @@ static void _z_tcp_zephyr_close(_z_sys_net_socket_t *sock) {
 }
 
 static size_t _z_tcp_zephyr_read(_z_sys_net_socket_t sock, uint8_t *ptr, size_t len) {
+#if !defined(CONFIG_NET_CONTEXT_RCVTIMEO)
+    // Without CONFIG_NET_CONTEXT_RCVTIMEO, SO_RCVTIMEO is rejected and recv() would block the lease job.
+    struct zsock_pollfd pfd = {.fd = sock._fd, .events = ZSOCK_POLLIN};
+    if (zsock_poll(&pfd, 1, Z_CONFIG_SOCKET_TIMEOUT) <= 0) {
+        return SIZE_MAX;
+    }
+#endif
     ssize_t rb = recv(sock._fd, ptr, len, 0);
     if (rb < (ssize_t)0) {
         return SIZE_MAX;
